<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prithvideva II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1135–<a href="/years/1165">1165</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prithvideva II was a king of the Kalachuri dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ratanpur">Ratanpur</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh">Chhattisgarh</a> in the 12th century. He extended the kingdom and fought the Eastern Gangas of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinga">Kalinga</a>, and numerous inscriptions and coins survive from his reign. The Kalachuris of Ratanpur were Shaiva patrons of temples and tanks at Ratanpur and Malhar.</p></div>
